# Phase 5: Application Integration & Security Hardening

## Objective

Transform the deployed Employee Management API from a basic
stateless service into a functional AWS-backed application and
secure the communication between the application and its supporting
cloud services.

Phase 4 established the AWS infrastructure and successfully deployed
the containerized API through ECS Fargate and an Application Load
Balancer.

Phase 5 connects the application to the data and storage services
already deployed and introduces application and cloud security
controls before formal security assessment begins.

## Current Architecture

Internet
   ↓
Application Load Balancer
   ↓
ECS Fargate
   ↓
Employee Management API
   │
   ├── Amazon RDS PostgreSQL
   ├── Amazon S3
   └── AWS Secrets Manager

CloudWatch and CloudTrail provide logging and audit visibility.

## Phase 5 Tasks

- [ ] Connect the Employee API to RDS PostgreSQL
- [ ] Retrieve database credentials from AWS Secrets Manager
- [ ] Create the employee database schema
- [ ] Implement employee CRUD operations
- [ ] Validate persistent employee storage
- [ ] Integrate employee document storage with Amazon S3
- [ ] Review ECS task IAM permissions
- [ ] Validate network security boundaries
- [ ] Add application input validation
- [ ] Add authentication and authorization
- [ ] Review application and CloudWatch logging
- [ ] Validate secrets are not exposed in source code or container images
- [ ] Perform Phase 5 security validation

## Employee API

The target API will support:

GET    /api/employees
GET    /api/employees/:id
POST   /api/employees
PUT    /api/employees/:id
DELETE /api/employees/:id

## Target Data Flow

Client
  ↓
Application Load Balancer
  ↓
Employee API
  ↓
AWS Secrets Manager
  ↓
RDS PostgreSQL

Employee documents will follow:

Client
  ↓
Employee API
  ↓
Amazon S3

## Security Goals

The application should:

- Never expose the PostgreSQL database directly to the Internet.
- Never store database credentials in application source code.
- Retrieve sensitive credentials securely from Secrets Manager.
- Restrict AWS access using the ECS task IAM role.
- Restrict database access to the application security group.
- Validate user-controlled input.
- Produce useful application logs without leaking secrets.
- Maintain private S3 document storage.
- Establish an authorization boundary around employee data.

## Phase 5 Completion Criteria

Phase 5 is complete when an employee can be created through the
public API, persisted in PostgreSQL, retrieved through the API,
updated and deleted, while AWS access, credentials, network paths,
and application controls have been validated and hardened.
